{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "GEN",
  "chapter": 44,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he commanded the steward of his house, saying, Fill the men's sacks ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " food, as much as they can carry, and put every man's money in his sack's mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And put my cup, the silver cup, in the sack's mouth of the youngest, and his corn money: and he did according to the word that Joseph had spoken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As soon as the morning was light, the men were sent away, they, and their asses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " when they had gone out of the city, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " were not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " far off, Joseph said to his steward, Arise, follow after the men; and when thou dost overtake them, say to them, Why have ye rewarded evil for good?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the cup",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in which my lord drinketh, and by which indeed he divineth? ye have done evil in so doing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he overtook them, and he spoke to them these same words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they said to him, Why saith my lord these words? Far be it from us that thy servants should do according to this thing:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, the money which we found in our sacks' mouths, we brought again to thee from the land of Canaan: how then should we steal from thy lord's house silver or gold?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With whom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "soever",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of thy servants it shall be found, both let him die, and we also will be my lord's bond-men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, Now also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "let",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " according to your words: he with whom it shall be found, shall be my servant; and ye shall be blameless.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they speedily took down every man his sack to the ground, and opened every man his sack.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he searched, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " began at the eldest, and left at the youngest: and the cup was found in Benjamin's sack.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they rent their clothes, and loaded every man his ass, and returned to the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Judah and his brethren came to Joseph's house, (for he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yet there:) and they fell before him on the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Joseph said to them, What deed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this that ye have done? knew ye not that such a man as I can certainly divine?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Judah said, What shall we say to my lord? what shall we speak? or how shall we clear ourselves? God hath found out the iniquity of thy servants: behold we ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my lord's servants, both we, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " also with whom the cup is found.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, Far be it from me that I should do so: the man in whose hand the cup is found, he shall be my servant; and as for you, go in peace to your father.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Judah came near to him, and said, Oh my lord, let thy servant, I pray thee, speak a word in my lord's ears, and let not thy anger burn against thy servant; for thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " even as Pharaoh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My lord asked his servants, saying, Have ye a father, or a brother?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And we said to my lord, We have a father, an old man, and a child of his old age, a little one: and his brother is dead, and he alone is left of his mother, and his father loveth him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou saidst to thy servants, Bring him down to me, that I may set my eyes upon him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And we said to my lord, The lad cannot leave his father; for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he should leave his father, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his father",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " would die.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou saidst to thy servants, Except your youngest brother shall come down with you, ye shall see my face no more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, when we came to thy servant, my father, we told him the words of my lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And our father said, Go again; buy us a little food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And we said, We cannot go down: if our youngest brother shall be with us, then will we go down; for we may not see the man's face, except our youngest brother shall ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thy servant my father, said to us, Ye know that my wife bore me two ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "sons",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the one went out from me, and I said, Surely he is torn in pieces; and I have not seen him since:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if ye take this also from me, and mischief shall befall him, ye will bring down my gray hairs with sorrow to the grave.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now therefore, when I come to thy servant my father, and the lad is not with us; (seeing that his life is bound up in the lad's life)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It shall come to pass, when he seeth that the lad ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that he will die: and thy servants will bring down the gray hairs of thy servant our father, with sorrow to the grave.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thy servant became surety for the lad to my father, saying, If I bring him not to thee, then I will bear the blame to my father for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now therefore, I pray thee, let thy servant abide instead of the lad, a bond-man to my lord; and let the lad return with his brethren.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.44.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.44.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For how shall I return to my father, and the lad ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not with me? lest perhaps I see the evil that shall come on my father.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
